<http://lblod.data.gift/id/conceptscheme/ai-advisory-board-model-levels> a skos:ConceptScheme ;
  skos:prefLabel "AI advisory board model guidelines" ;
  skos:description "A concept scheme that defines the different levels of AI models as defined by the AI advisory board." .

<http://lblod.data.gift/id/concept/ai-model-level/small-trained-model> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:prefLabel "Small trained model" ;
  skos:description "Train smaller models (non-LLM) on datasets using available pre-trained models (e.g. transformers from the huggingface), when labels are not available, you can make use of external providers of LLMs to generate labels (and store this generated data for provenance as linked data)." ;
  skos:notation "L1" ;
  skos:topConceptOf <http://lblod.data.gift/id/conceptscheme/ai-advisory-board-model-levels> .

<http://lblod.data.gift/id/concept/ai-model-level/local-os-llm> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:prefLabel "Local OS LLM" ;
  skos:description "If the problem can not be solved using smaller models, document the motivation why only a LLM can provide a solution for your use case and prove that the solution is business-aligned. As a next step, consider the of an open source LLM which can be hosted and evaluated locally on the infrastructure of Digiteam. Adhering to the Flanders AI strategy we defined a set of criteria for each of the six principles to evaluate popular OS LLM families. When choosing a model, consult the scores, and try to stick models which have the higher scores. If models with bad scores are used, there must be a very clear motivation on why the same can not be achieved by models families with higher scores. Note that the scores can not be summed up and serve as a ranking, they provide a general assessment of a model family." ;
  skos:notation "L2" ;
  skos:topConceptOf <http://lblod.data.gift/id/conceptscheme/ai-advisory-board-model-levels> .

<http://lblod.data.gift/id/concept/ai-model-level/external-os-llm> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:prefLabel "External OS LLM" ;
  skos:description "If your application can not run on an OS LLM because it is too large to run economically on a dedicated server, and you can not achieve results with smaller OS LLM, verify if you can run the larger OS LLM on our list of OS SaaS LLM Providers. This is preferable over using proprietary SaaS LLMs, because we maintain model ownership (e.g., we have the weights and could theoretically buy a bigger server should we want to)." ;
  skos:notation "L3" ;
  skos:topConceptOf <http://lblod.data.gift/id/conceptscheme/ai-advisory-board-model-levels> .

<http://lblod.data.gift/id/concept/ai-model-level/external-proprietary-llm> a skos:Concept ;
  skos:prefLabel "External proprietary LLM" ;
  skos:description "If none of this is sufficient, go with a proprietary SaaS LLM Provider from our list. We don't have the LLM model, they can revoke or alter the LLM model and our application breaks. This means it should always be considered as the last option. " ;
  skos:notation "L4" ;
  skos:topConceptOf <http://lblod.data.gift/id/conceptscheme/ai-advisory-board-model-levels> .

